    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Mimi the Travel Bee",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117542156103217041817/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJufuwpf_TeMGCkA-nEYnaOLVii1vwkfQAGJxD8Nj6h7VDhyw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 4,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "Great Service & Tasty Food, But Pricey\n\nHad a great experience at Carlos & Pepes in Vaudreuil! First off, the service was excellent—our server, Calina, was truly amazing. She was kind, efficient, and thoughtful, which made our visit even more enjoyable.\n\nThe food was good, but I have to say the pricing felt a bit steep—$29 for three shrimp tacos with rice is quite high. That said, everything tasted great! I especially liked the Inferno Tacos, which were packed with flavor, and their fries were surprisingly good. The kids’ menu was decent, but I’d love to see more healthy options for little ones. More vegan or vegetarian choices would also be a great addition to the menu.\n\nThe atmosphere was pleasant, and we had a great dinner. We went early to beat the dinner rush, which was a good call—by 6:30, the place was pretty full.\n\nTried their mojito, and it was really nice—I’d definitely recommend it. Overall, a solid spot for a night out, with fantastic service, but the pricing knocks it down a star.",
        "time": 1739651954,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Roley Liu",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112341051539785993112/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLm39DTIPYm2c2SCsJ1xIINPDWekGgQijr2YmICFPpKTvmhdA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "Update. We came back a few days after our first visit. We were seated before the supper rush started. We had to ask for someone to take our order as no one came around. Then they forgot our order of beer. We weren't able to flag our server to get our beer.\nAs for the food, we ordered the pastor and the shredded chicken bowl.\nIt will be a long time before we go back again.\n\nOriginal post. We had the chili con carne with chips as the starter, very tender beef, really nice flavor! For the main course, we had the shredded chicken burrito and the BBQ Chipotle chicken bowl.",
        "time": 1723378301,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Juliet Martin",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113581764729625935388/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWe8dfsQn5X6K7rGUCUIS-xLEU0FNncJAebMcpCynPpYcSJUQAeKA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 4,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "We had fish tacos and ribs tonight. The food was okay. Not great but not bad either. But the service was exceptional. Our waiter was Chris and he gave us a warm welcome . His upbeat friendliness made our dining experience fun. His genuine smile was infectious and his knowledge of the menu and bar menu was thoroughly helpful.",
        "time": 1713492776,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Joanne groves",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112051182088243070371/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKOGgF_jOrgZgw5HGS-9JoFOJeVyywAlrDCK5FtSXExKcv_wQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
